From: Stealth Build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 03/05] WebGL: never leak a software renderer

DESIGN DECISION (v146 CloakBrowser parity): the CyberPunch wrapper already
spoofs WebGL vendor/renderer PER PROFILE via JS injection (FingerprintDb).
So this native patch must NOT hard-pin one GPU for every profile - that
would override the per-profile spoof and REDUCE realism. Instead it is a
guarded fallback: return the REAL driver string unchanged (so the JS layer
can still override it per profile), and ONLY substitute a common discrete
GPU when the real renderer is a software rasterizer (SwiftShader / llvmpipe
/ Mesa / "Software"), which is the one thing that would betray a headless /
GPU-less box.

FIX vs. source doc: the doc's diff had IDENTICAL '-'/'+' lines (a no-op) and
fabricated context. Real Blink resolves UNMASKED_* via GetUnmaskedString().

>>> VERIFY on tag 151.0.7922.108: confirm the helper name/signature in
    third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
    and adjust the @@ context if it drifted. CI uses `git apply --3way`.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
@@ WebGLRenderingContextBase::GetUnmaskedString(GLenum name)
 String WebGLRenderingContextBase::GetUnmaskedString(GLenum name) {
-  return String(ContextGL()->GetString(name));
+  String real = String(ContextGL()->GetString(name));
+  // Stealth: only rewrite when a software rasterizer would leak. Real GPUs
+  // pass through untouched so the wrapper's per-profile spoof stays authoritative.
+  String lower = real.LowerASCII();
+  const bool software = lower.Contains("swiftshader") || lower.Contains("llvmpipe") ||
+                        lower.Contains("software") || lower.Contains("mesa") ||
+                        lower.Contains("microsoft basic render");
+  if (software) {
+    if (name == GL_VENDOR)
+      return String("Google Inc. (NVIDIA)");
+    if (name == GL_RENDERER)
+      return String(
+          "ANGLE (NVIDIA, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Direct3D11 vs_5_0 ps_5_0, "
+          "D3D11)");
+  }
+  return real;
 }
